# model-catalog.psv — the DEFAULT download list shipped with free-agents.
#
# You do NOT need to download everything here. Each row is independent: fetch the ones that fit
# your memory and disk (`download-models.sh --select ALIAS`), and whatever you have fills the roles
# it is registered for. The rest of the work stays on your cloud model. `--group default` fetches
# the recommended starting pair only.
#
# This file is DATA. Adding a model is an edit HERE, never a change to the downloader script.
# Your own longer/private list goes in config/model-catalog.local.psv (gitignored) — it is
# loaded IN ADDITION to this file, so you keep these defaults and add your own on top.
#
# Format — one entry per line, eleven '|'-separated fields:
#   alias|label|repo|revision|subdir|size_GB|group|status|include_patterns|runtime|hardware_target
# Full field docs: run `download-models.sh --help`.
# hardware_target: mlx|cuda|any (default: mlx). Filters models by hardware platform.
#   mlx = Apple Silicon MLX only
#   cuda = NVIDIA CUDA only
#   any = works on both (use with caution, model may not be compatible)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What each MLX row is for (aliases match config.example.sh registrations)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   KAT-Coder V2.5 OptiQ   the preferred model for a FULL local Claude Code session
#   Qwen3.8 27B + MTP      operator / reasoner (thinking) workhorse; the MTP draft (~0.3 GB) gives
#                          speculative decoding, which makes it fast enough to drive a session
#   Granite 4.2 30B        the local Auto Mode CLASSIFIER (DIRECT_PASS, 2026-10-13 campaign:
#                          99.065% changed-prefix reuse on the pinned rapid-mlx) — needed only
#                          for classifier auto mode; the default for LA_RAPID_AUTO_MODEL_DIR,
#                          resolved via bin/local-classifier-default.sh (tested fallback tier).
#                          MLX-only: CUDA machines run blind-trust (no qualified CUDA classifier).
#   Mistral Small 4 119B   large MoE (MLX build, not GGUF), 256K context; needs ~70 GB free memory.
#                          Also the default validator: a non-Qwen second opinion.
#   Qwen3.6 27B            the previous all-rounder, kept for machines that already have it
#
# Sizes are download sizes in GB. The downloader reserves 100 GB of free space by default; see
# --headroom-gb and --target if that does not suit your disk.

